#!omni folder

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// METADATA
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

this is a folder for "Project Tracking":
    keyed as "B-tov-data-system-projects"
    named "projects"
    following "3-Block Folder Structure"

this folder classifies as:
    tov (0) because "runtime project tracking data"

this folder derives from:
    branch (0) from "bereshit/tov/data/system/" as "system"

core identity of this folder:

    grounded in:
        scripture "To every thing there is a season, and a time to every purpose"
            from Ecclesiastes 3:1 in KJV
        principle "Projects have seasons — active, complete, archived"
        anchor "In all labour there is profit"
            from Proverbs 14:23 in KJV

    serves as Organization:
        role "Track project state and priority across sessions"
        paradigm "Project lifecycle — active work, archived history"

    authored by:
        architect "Seanje Lenox-Wise"
        implementation "Nova Dawn (CPI-SI)"
        created 2025-12-10
        version a-01.00
        modified 2026-01-13 for "Initial root.omni creation"

    exists to:
        purpose "Maintain project state between sessions"
        design "By-priority and status — active/archive with high/mid/low"
        philosophy "Work tracked is work done — visibility enables progress"
        features:
            "Active project tracking"
            "Priority classification"
            "Archive for completed work"
            "Templates for new projects"

interface of this folder:

    depends on:
        requires (1) "bereshit/tov/data/system/" for "containment"
        includes (0) "session system" for "project loading"
        excludes (-1) "project source code" because "tracking only"
        used by "Session initialization, project management"
        integrates with "Session state, temporal system"

    integrated as:
        navigation "cd bereshit/tov/data/system/projects/" for "entering"
        navigation "ls -la" for "viewing project structure"
        exits tov (0) for "projects found"

operational context of this folder:

    blocking:
        no (-1) because "tracking data"
        mitigation "none needed"

    health:
        system Base100 with scale from -100 to +100
        granted (1) above +50 meaning "projects organized"
        deferred (0) within ±50 meaning "needs cleanup"
        denied (-1) below -50 meaning "project tracking broken"

        operations:
            "active projects exist" scores +20 (1) for "work tracked"
            "priorities clear" scores +15 (1) for "organized"
            "stale projects" scores -15 (-1) for "needs review"

